/**
 * A daily supplemental-service plan: which extra buses are allocated and exactly what each one
 * does, fixed at the start of the service day.
 *
 * A plan is deliberately a **separate contract from its results** ({@link SimResults}). The same
 * plan evaluated against different demand would give different results, so conflating the two
 * would make it impossible to say what was being compared.
 *
 * **What a plan does not contain.** Core service is referenced by id
 * ({@link SimPlan#coreTripIds}) and never modified — the plan adds supplemental capacity on top of
 * MTD's fixed routes and does not compete with or override MTD's own routing. A plan is advisory:
 * nothing in this system dispatches a bus.
 *
 * **Frozen at the cutoff.** {@link SimPlan#eventIdsVisibleToPlanner} records exactly which events
 * the planner was allowed to see. Once built, the plan is executed as-is: there is no live
 * rerouting, because a poor mid-day routing decision is hard to recover from and the team rejected
 * it.
 */
type SimPlan {

  /** Stable deterministic id, e.g. `plan_<scenarioId>_<allocation>` or `plan_<scenarioId>_baseline`. */
  planId: !string

  /**
   * Whether this is the mock old-model baseline or a candidate recommendation.
   *
   * `MockOldModelBaseline` is fixed core service with **zero** extra buses. It is labelled "mock"
   * everywhere because no historical MTD model was available to integrate — it does not reproduce
   * one. By construction the zero-extra-bus candidate and this baseline produce identical results,
   * which is asserted rather than assumed.
   */
  planKind: !string enum('MockOldModelBaseline','Candidate')

  /** Id of the {@link SimScenario} this plan is for. */
  scenarioId: !string

  /**
   * Number of extra buses allocated, from 0 to {@link SimScenario#maxExtraBuses}. Counts buses
   * *allocated*, including any that end up idle — see {@link SimBusItinerary#isIdle}.
   */
  allocation: !int

  /** One itinerary per allocated bus; see {@link SimBusItinerary}. Empty for the baseline. */
  extraBusItineraries: [SimBusItinerary]

  /**
   * Ids of the {@link SimCoreTrip}s in force, recorded to make the invariance explicit: this list
   * is identical in the baseline and in every candidate.
   */
  coreTripIds: [string]

  /** The {@link SimScenario#planningCutoff} this plan was built against. */
  planningCutoff: !datetime

  /**
   * Ids of exactly those {@link SimEvent}s with {@link SimEvent#knownAt} at or before
   * {@link SimPlan#planningCutoff} — the planner's entire knowledge of the day.
   *
   * Recorded on the plan so the no-hindsight property is auditable after the fact, not merely
   * asserted in prose. Any event realized by the engine and absent from this list is a disruption
   * the plan had to absorb blind.
   */
  eventIdsVisibleToPlanner: [string]

  /** Plan-level notes: the bottlenecks targeted, buses deliberately left idle, candidates rejected as infeasible. */
  explanations: [string]

  /**
   * Version of the planning heuristic that produced this plan, e.g.
   * `greedy-bottleneck-benefit-cost-1.0`. Lets two plans in an export be told apart when the
   * heuristic changes.
   */
  heuristicVersion: string

  /**
   * Feasibility findings for this plan — a stop closed under a planned call, a bus withdrawn after
   * the cutoff, a trip that would overrun {@link SimExtraBus#availableTo}.
   *
   * Reported, never repaired: a plan that is infeasible against the realized day keeps its issues
   * and earns the metrics that follow from them.
   */
  validation: SimValidationReport

  /** Total allocated-bus operating cost, in {@link SimCostConfig#currency}; the sum over {@link SimPlan#extraBusItineraries}. */
  totalOperatingCost: double

  /** Count of allocated buses that run at least one trip. Always <= {@link SimPlan#allocation}. */
  busesUsed: int

  /** Count of allocated buses that run nothing; `allocation - busesUsed`. */
  busesIdle: int
}
